":0.5283,"def_epa_per_play":-0.397},{"week":6,"opponent":"SEA","home":true,"pf":17.0,"pa":14.0,"off_snaps":56,"epa_per_play":-0.1438,"pass_rate":0.5179,"pass_rate_neutral":0.4375,"def_epa_per_play":-0.08701},{"week":7,"opponent":"ARI","home":false,"pf":30.0,"pa":16.0,"off_snaps":54,"epa_per_play":0.2019,"pass_rate":0.5556,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6053,"def_epa_per_play":-0.113}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2022,"team":"JAX","distance":0.4289,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"NE","distance":0.5055,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"GB","distance":0.5142,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Matt LaFleur"},{"season":2023,"team":"JAX","distance":0.5409,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"NYG","distance":0.6106,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Brian Daboll"}],"defense":[{"season":2025,"team":"IND","distance":0.1524,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Lou Anarumo"},{"season":2025,"team":"NE","distance":0.2021,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"GB","distance":0.2478,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"KC","distance":0.2929,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Steve Spagnuolo"},{"season":2025,"team":"NYG","distance":0.3571,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Broncos are 5-2 through week 7 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 144 to 141. The defense has done most of the work, ranking 7th in EPA allowed while the offense sits 22nd in EPA per play.","offense":"The Broncos offense has struggled, ranking 25th or worse in three of the five main efficiency measures. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Bo Nix has run the passing game, with Jaylen Waddle leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Broncos have one of the best defenses in the league this season, ranking 7th or better in three of the five main efficiency measures. The one weak spot has been EPA allowed per rush, where they rank 28th. Nik Bonitto has led the way with 3.5 sacks. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is an eight man box rate that ranks 8th highest in the league.","special":"The Broncos have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 80% of field goals, which is a little below average. Their salary cap was spread across positions in a fairly typical way. Their offensive line was among the oldest in the league.","players":"Bo Nix has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,271 yards. Jaylen Waddle has been the clear top target with 23% of the looks and 276 receiving yards. J.K. Dobbins has handled most of the work in the backfield with 60% of the carries. On defense, Zach Allen leads the team with 4.5 sacks and Brandon Jones has picked off 2 passes.","coaching":"Davis Webb is calling the offense and Vance Joseph is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2022 Jaguars and the 2022 Patriots. Their defense looks most like the 2025 Colts under Lou Anarumo and the 2025 Patriots.","trends":"The offense went from 10th in EPA per play in 2025 to 22nd so far this season, a big step back. The defense moved from 6th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 7th so far this season, about where it was. The biggest change in approach was pre-snap motion rate, which went from 47% to 61%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}